-- WAY W0 (wrong, kept to show why): write the retrospective Notification as if it were an ordinary amendment
-- with a commencement date, with no reader gate at all.
--
-- The text that governs is chosen by the day whose law we are using (RULES EFFECTIVE DATE), which follows the
-- conduct day.  The Notification is given its deemed commencement, 1 January 2011, and nothing else.
-- It cannot tell a reader before 31 October 2012 from a reader after it: both are told the television is gone.
-- Printed output is in alt-w0-no-publication-gate.out; walkthrough step 7.
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
TIMEZONE IS "Asia/Singapore"

DECLARE `Version of the First Schedule` IS ONE OF
    `the First Schedule of three items`
    `the First Schedule of the TVRO system only`

`the text, read at the rule-effective date` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `RULES EFFECTIVE DATE` BELOW (Date 31 7 2003)
           THEN REFUSE "not covered: the conduct day is before the first deposited edition (31 July 2003)"
           IF `RULES EFFECTIVE DATE` AT LEAST (Date 1 1 2011)
           THEN `the First Schedule of the TVRO system only`
           OTHERWISE `the First Schedule of three items`

GIVEN conduct IS A DATE
      reading IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Version of the First Schedule`
`the text under this way` MEANS
    `EVAL AS OF SYSTEM TIME` reading (`EVAL UNDER VALID TIME` conduct `the text, read at the rule-effective date`)

-- BEGIN GENERATED PAIRS (build-walkthrough.py: the same conduct-day and reading-day pairs in every file)
